==== Arm A: the commit reached the log and only the response was lost ====
-- the acknowledged rows must survive; deleting the data files here is the data loss
plain: reported as unknown outcome: yes
plain: original error chained: yes
plain: retained files logged: yes
plain: retained files named: 1 (expected 1)
plain: sum(c0) after reopen: 15 (expected 15)
plain: rows after reopen: [0,1,2,3,4,5] (expected [0,1,2,3,4,5])
plain: data files kept: 1 (expected 1)
plain: commits in log: 2 (expected 2)
partitioned: reported as unknown outcome: yes
partitioned: original error chained: yes
partitioned: retained files logged: yes
partitioned: retained files named: 2 (expected 2)
partitioned: retained files carry the physical partition dirs: yes/yes, encoded form absent: no
partitioned: sum(c0) after reopen: 15 (expected 15)
partitioned: rows after reopen: [0,1,2,3,4,5] (expected [0,1,2,3,4,5])
partitioned: data files kept: 2 (expected 2)
partitioned: commits in log: 2 (expected 2)

==== Arm B: the commit never reached the log ====
-- the data files are unreferenced for certain, so they must still be cleaned up
plain: failed for the injected reason: yes
plain: reported as unknown outcome: no
plain: data files removed: 0 (expected 0)
plain: commits in log: 1 (expected 1)
plain: rows readable: [] (expected [])
partitioned: failed for the injected reason: yes
partitioned: reported as unknown outcome: no
partitioned: data files removed: 0 (expected 0)
partitioned: commits in log: 1 (expected 1)
partitioned: rows readable: [] (expected [])

==== Arm C: the retried PUT conflicted with the entry its own first attempt stored ====
-- that entry adds this INSERT's data files, so the commit took effect and the INSERT succeeds
plain: INSERT failed: no
plain: sum(c0) after reopen: 15 (expected 15)
plain: data files kept: 1 (expected 1)
plain: commits in log: 2 (expected 2)
partitioned: INSERT failed: no
partitioned: sum(c0) after reopen: 15 (expected 15)
partitioned: data files kept: 2 (expected 2)
partitioned: commits in log: 2 (expected 2)
empty: reported as unknown outcome: yes
empty: commits in log: 2 (expected 2)

==== Arm D: a non-conflict error quoting an object key that contains the conflict text ====
-- the commit is durable, as in arm A, so its data files must be kept
marker: the error quotes the key: yes
marker: reported as unknown outcome: yes
marker: sum(c0) after reopen: 15 (expected 15)
marker: data files kept: 1 (expected 1)
marker: commits in log: 2 (expected 2)

==== control: an INSERT with no failpoint commits and reads back ====
control: sum(c0): 15 (expected 15)
control: data files: 1 (expected 1)
control: commits in log: 2 (expected 2)
